note The walk: roots in list order, then each step's children sorted by the caller's key with list order breaking ties. The views pass the line of the parent's slice that names the child, so siblings read in the order the code calls them; the plain tree_order passes a constant. A step whose parent index is out of range or is itself counts as a root, and steps caught in a parent cycle are visited once each, as roots, after everything else.

